---
import Shell from '../layouts/shell.astro';

const birthdate = "1997-08-09T07:00:00Z";
const ageDiff = new Date(Date.now() - new Date(birthdate).getTime());
const age = ageDiff.getUTCFullYear() - 1970;
---

<Shell title="skiddle@web ~/about" description="About Jeff (Skiddle) — night-shift DevOps engineer in Bangkok, building platforms, automation, and open internet infrastructure.">
  <div class="prose max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-5 md:px-0 space-y-4">
    <h1>About me</h1>

    <p class="mt-2">
      I'm Jeff — also known as <strong>Skiddle</strong>. I'm a {age}-year-old DevOps engineer
      based in Bangkok, Thailand. By day (or rather, by night — I work the graveyard shift)
      I build platforms, automate operations, and keep infrastructure running smoothly across
      cloud and self-hosted environments.
    </p>

    <p>
      My stack is Go, PHP/Laravel, Node.js, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, Redis, Docker, and Kubernetes.
      I deploy on Cloudflare, AWS, and self-hosted. I'm also into open protocols — the ATProtocol
      ecosystem in particular — and I run a small personal mesh of self-hosted services from
      my homelab setup.
    </p>

    <p>
      I like shipping small tools that remove toil. Reliability, security, and cost efficiency
      are my priorities. I automate everything I can, and I'm always curious about new ways
      to make systems better.
    </p>

    <h2>On the Skiddle Ecosystem</h2>

    <p>
      This site — <strong>skiddle.id</strong> — is my corner of the internet.
      I post about what I'm working on, what I'm learning, and occasionally things that
      have nothing to do with tech. The blog is powered by ATProtocol, which means posts
      are decentralized and you can follow via Bluesky.
    </p>

    <p>
      I also run a small collection of personal projects — servers, bots, infrastructure
      tools — most of which you'll find on GitHub.
    </p>

    <h2>Personal stuff</h2>

    <p>
      I have a bit of ADHD, but it doesn't get in the way of the work. Outside of tech,
      I game, read, and generally exist at odd hours. I'm a night person — go figure.
    </p>

    <p>
      I believe in open internet, open protocols, and owning your own data. I also believe
      you should be able to run your own infrastructure if you want to.
    </p>

    <p>
      For a detailed breakdown of my hardware, software, and tools, check out my
      <a href="/uses">Uses page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Shell>
